 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi, how are you holding up?",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.32,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_16"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Kind of tired, honestly.",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.95,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Can I tune my guitar without a tuner? Mine's broken.",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "block": "music.dlg5",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Yes, with the fifth fret method. If one string is roughly right, you can tune the others to it.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 0.84,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "music.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "How does that work?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.79,
   "block": "music.dlg5",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Press the low string at the fifth fret, and the note should match the next string played open. Adjust that next string until they sound the same.",
   "est_sec": 8.47,
   "gap_before": 0.33,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "music.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Lucas, did you put the red sock in with the whites again?",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 2.99,
   "block": "nq_home_001",
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "other_name",
   "phrasing": "nq_home_001",
   "name_pos": "start",
   "addressee": "Lucas"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "other",
   "text": "Maybe. Is everything pink?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.87,
   "block": "nq_home_001"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "And then keep",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.55,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "music.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "going across the strings?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 2.78,
   "block": "music.dlg5",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Exactly, all the way across. Except the second thinnest string, for that one you use the fourth fret instead of the fifth.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.72,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "music.dlg5"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Why's that one different?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.67,
   "block": "music.dlg5",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It's just how guitars are tuned, that gap is a bit smaller. Also, a free tuner app on your phone does the job in a pinch.",
   "est_sec": 8.16,
   "gap_before": 0.73,
   "role": "reply",
